(1115227, 132507, 23458, '<td valign="top">Jeremy Lelii right ? This is certainly not a bad shot - but I''ve seen a couple of others of yours in forums that beat this hands down. Nice to see you try a slightly different approach to what is a fairly tired formula,  but I think the lighting at the top  of the frame is a bit harsh, and the mauve (or whatever the heck that colour is called) background doesn''t really work for me. I do like the shadows a lot though. Still, this is a 6 from me - a shame cos I''ve seen a couple of your shots that would definately warrant and eight or nine.</td>', 'Jeremy Lelii right ? This is certainly not a bad shot - but I''ve seen a couple of others of yours in forums that beat this hands down. Nice to see you try a slightly different approach to what is a fairly tired formula,  but I think the lighting at the top  of the frame is a bit harsh, and the mauve (or whatever the heck that colour is called) background doesn''t really work for me. I do like the shadows a lot though. Still, this is a 6 from me - a shame cos I''ve seen a couple of your shots that would definately warrant and eight or nine.', '2005-01-17 17:33:53.000000', NULL, 1),
