(1121369, 136823, 3032, '<td valign="top">Hi mon Cheri,<br/> <br/>I had done my voting and I had no clue what photograph could possibly be yours. :)<br/>So what to do? Pbase! :) I had given this an 8 before I checked and I am not going to change it.  O :-)<br/> <br/>Great photo, it has such strong composition and lighting. The guitar leads me trough the frame and the hands show me what''s going on. The beard sheds some light on the character that is playing, it leaves something to the fantasy of the viewer. That way the viewer can decice for himself if this is a country, heavy-metal, bluess, jazz or pop player. Fits everyones views.<br/>I like the darkness in the background and on the face of the guitar body, it helps to direct the eye to the more important parts: the hands and the long bit supporting the strings. Shame about the highlight blowout of the string tensioners, but you''d need another camera and a lot of underexposure with shadow correction to get any detail back. It distracts a little, but should be accepted as the limitation of photography.<br/> <br/>I must say, it sure is one of the best I''ve seen from you in 2004 and I hope it does well. Let''s rock in 2005!<br/>See ya!</td>', 'Hi mon Cheri, I had done my voting and I had no clue what photograph could possibly be yours. :)So what to do? Pbase! :) I had given this an 8 before I checked and I am not going to change it.  O :-) Great photo, it has such strong composition and lighting. The guitar leads me trough the frame and the hands show me what''s going on. The beard sheds some light on the character that is playing, it leaves something to the fantasy of the viewer. That way the viewer can decice for himself if this is a country, heavy-metal, bluess, jazz or pop player. Fits everyones views.I like the darkness in the background and on the face of the guitar body, it helps to direct the eye to the more important parts: the hands and the long bit supporting the strings. Shame about the highlight blowout of the string tensioners, but you''d need another camera and a lot of underexposure with shadow correction to get any detail back. It distracts a little, but should be accepted as the limitation of photography. I must say, it sure is one of the best I''ve seen from you in 2004 and I hope it does well. Let''s rock in 2005!See ya!', '2005-01-20 12:46:47.000000', NULL, 1),
