(1126765, 134735, 23394, '<td valign="top">what an interesting image.  i think you probably have a knack for coming up with some pretty fun stuff, and am looking forward to your other work.  in the meantime, though, take a few moments to work through the tutorials related to preparing images for challenges.  i think you might be losing points unnecessarily due to both image size and quality.  in challenges of this size, voters are not very forgiving when it comes to simple things like size and quality.  nothing is worse than having a great image that comes across poorly.  if your scores and comments here don''t meet your expectation, please don''t take it personally.  just look at this as a starting point, and keep on shooting and submitting!  good luck in this and all the coming challenges!</td>', 'what an interesting image.  i think you probably have a knack for coming up with some pretty fun stuff, and am looking forward to your other work.  in the meantime, though, take a few moments to work through the tutorials related to preparing images for challenges.  i think you might be losing points unnecessarily due to both image size and quality.  in challenges of this size, voters are not very forgiving when it comes to simple things like size and quality.  nothing is worse than having a great image that comes across poorly.  if your scores and comments here don''t meet your expectation, please don''t take it personally.  just look at this as a starting point, and keep on shooting and submitting!  good luck in this and all the coming challenges!', '2005-01-23 10:34:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1126774, 136635, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, i''m sure you''re getting hammered by the kid-cops, so i won''t pile on.  if your scores and comments here don''t meet your expectation, please don''t take it personally.  just look at this as a starting point, and keep on shooting and submitting!  remember, one of the ''challenges'' is to submit images that will appeal to a broad base of viewers.  while this is a great image for your scrapbook, it probably will not excite too many people who don''t have an emotional tie to the child.  on the other hand, if you had her standing on the rock, looking towards the mountains, and you composed it with her in a lower corner, you''d have an image that would speak volumes!  children can be GREAT subjects, but only if you use them to help your image tell a story.  hope this helps some.  good luck in this and all the coming challenges!</td>', 'ok, i''m sure you''re getting hammered by the kid-cops, so i won''t pile on.  if your scores and comments here don''t meet your expectation, please don''t take it personally.  just look at this as a starting point, and keep on shooting and submitting!  remember, one of the ''challenges'' is to submit images that will appeal to a broad base of viewers.  while this is a great image for your scrapbook, it probably will not excite too many people who don''t have an emotional tie to the child.  on the other hand, if you had her standing on the rock, looking towards the mountains, and you composed it with her in a lower corner, you''d have an image that would speak volumes!  children can be GREAT subjects, but only if you use them to help your image tell a story.  hope this helps some.  good luck in this and all the coming challenges!', '2005-01-23 10:39:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1126778, 136703, 23394, '<td valign="top">oh boy, you can almost feel the tension and uncertainty, trying to desparately remember the next note...  you have captured quite a moment here, and i hope it isn''t overlooked and blown by in this monster challenge.  good luck in this and the coming challenges!</td>', 'oh boy, you can almost feel the tension and uncertainty, trying to desparately remember the next note...  you have captured quite a moment here, and i hope it isn''t overlooked and blown by in this monster challenge.  good luck in this and the coming challenges!', '2005-01-23 10:40:51.000000', NULL, 1),
