(1126789, 132625, 11394, '<td valign="top">You did a great job with this photo. I like the desaturation, lighting and the expression on the girls face. The hair under her chin and a little white streak to to the right of her chin  is a little distracting. Very nice picture, good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'You did a great job with this photo. I like the desaturation, lighting and the expression on the girls face. The hair under her chin and a little white streak to to the right of her chin  is a little distracting. Very nice picture, good luck with the challenge.', '2005-01-23 10:46:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1126791, 136246, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, please bear with me.  voting this challenge is extremely difficult, not just because of the size, but because we are dealing with images that people consider their best.  it makes even constructive criticism hard...<br/> <br/>for all intents and purposes, this is a snapshot documentary image of one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world.  the question is not how this is going to score, but how would you shoot this subject again if you could go back next december?  the answer to that depends on how hard you push yourself to learn about your camera, composing images before you click, and processing them once you have them on your computer.  this is a great place to learn all these things, but you will have to also put up some of the silliness and less-than-tactful comments that come with a large, disparate community.<br/> <br/>if you aren''t happy with how this image is received, please don''t take it personally.  just look at it as a starting point for where you can go.  i hope you''re getting some good comments and suggestions.  good luck in this and the coming challenges!</td>', 'ok, please bear with me.  voting this challenge is extremely difficult, not just because of the size, but because we are dealing with images that people consider their best.  it makes even constructive criticism hard... for all intents and purposes, this is a snapshot documentary image of one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world.  the question is not how this is going to score, but how would you shoot this subject again if you could go back next december?  the answer to that depends on how hard you push yourself to learn about your camera, composing images before you click, and processing them once you have them on your computer.  this is a great place to learn all these things, but you will have to also put up some of the silliness and less-than-tactful comments that come with a large, disparate community. if you aren''t happy with how this image is received, please don''t take it personally.  just look at it as a starting point for where you can go.  i hope you''re getting some good comments and suggestions.  good luck in this and the coming challenges!', '2005-01-23 10:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
