(1153347, 132699, 14986, '<td valign="top">Pretty!  I think I would have either cropped it in closer, concentrating almost 100% on the flower and leaving out most of the background - or had it out a little more, increasing the background and placing the flower more in it''s element.   I guess I''m saying that I would change the composition.  It''s a lovely flower and a great subject to shoot.<br/> <br/>You might also consider bumping up the saturation just a bit, but not over doing it.  The nice thing about flowers is that they don''t get bored...take many shots from different angles and lighting.  Sometimes even backlighting on the petals looks cool.   Thanks for sharing!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Pretty!  I think I would have either cropped it in closer, concentrating almost 100% on the flower and leaving out most of the background - or had it out a little more, increasing the background and placing the flower more in it''s element.   I guess I''m saying that I would change the composition.  It''s a lovely flower and a great subject to shoot. You might also consider bumping up the saturation just a bit, but not over doing it.  The nice thing about flowers is that they don''t get bored...take many shots from different angles and lighting.  Sometimes even backlighting on the petals looks cool.   Thanks for sharing! ', '2005-02-06 13:17:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1153373, 132782, 9581, '<td valign="top">Shes so cute! Great quality image! Love the colors!</td>', 'Shes so cute! Great quality image! Love the colors!', '2005-02-06 13:48:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1154551, 133137, 23458, '<td valign="top">Well I think my original comment sums up how I feel about the placement of this shot. I am curious as to my initial question about whether anyone made any DQ requests (I''d be surprised if they didn''t - though disappointed if the site council seriously entertained them) - though I guess it''s not like its the kind of issue you''d have to supply proof over, so you likely wouldn''t know even if someone had. <br/> <br/>Anyway, I''m not going to rave over this again - I already did that, the only thing I can fault about the image is the title - I just think the almost comedic approach you have taken to titling this detracts from the sensuous air created by the shot itself. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Anders</td>', 'Well I think my original comment sums up how I feel about the placement of this shot. I am curious as to my initial question about whether anyone made any DQ requests (I''d be surprised if they didn''t - though disappointed if the site council seriously entertained them) - though I guess it''s not like its the kind of issue you''d have to supply proof over, so you likely wouldn''t know even if someone had.  Anyway, I''m not going to rave over this again - I already did that, the only thing I can fault about the image is the title - I just think the almost comedic approach you have taken to titling this detracts from the sensuous air created by the shot itself.  Cheers Anders', '2005-02-07 07:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
