(1716404, 132622, 17126, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by srbrubaker:</b></div><hr/><i> When does it cross from being a photo to being a photo-derived work of art?  It''s a subjective question but I think this one has crossed the line.  At first glance the colors are interesting, drammatic, striking. But seconds later we stop thinking about the picture and start thinking about the steps taken to make it.  Then we start wondering whether the sky really would have been better without that great blob of red.  Or with less of that inky blue.  And then, finally, the chartreuse of the grass begins to grate.  And we begin to wonder what it was we saw in the photo in that first second.  That was my experience, anyway.  For the first second or so, it was a real kick. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree completely. It goes from amazing to a sort of over saturated water color painting where color has no purpose.<br/> <br/>But it''s still a great picture, I just was shocked that this person described my feelings so perfectly.</td>', 'Originally posted by srbrubaker: When does it cross from being a photo to being a photo-derived work of art?  It''s a subjective question but I think this one has crossed the line.  At first glance the colors are interesting, drammatic, striking. But seconds later we stop thinking about the picture and start thinking about the steps taken to make it.  Then we start wondering whether the sky really would have been better without that great blob of red.  Or with less of that inky blue.  And then, finally, the chartreuse of the grass begins to grate.  And we begin to wonder what it was we saw in the photo in that first second.  That was my experience, anyway.  For the first second or so, it was a real kick.   I agree completely. It goes from amazing to a sort of over saturated water color painting where color has no purpose. But it''s still a great picture, I just was shocked that this person described my feelings so perfectly.', '2005-09-17 14:55:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1722100, 135805, 14986, '<td valign="top">This was the best of your series I think.  For me, the reason has mostly to do with the lighting of the face and the eyes.  I think in a portrait the eyes are so important.  This has a nice, natural feel to it, and the emphasis is on her face.  Very nice job.</td>', 'This was the best of your series I think.  For me, the reason has mostly to do with the lighting of the face and the eyes.  I think in a portrait the eyes are so important.  This has a nice, natural feel to it, and the emphasis is on her face.  Very nice job.', '2005-09-19 20:56:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1739607, 133785, 34659, '<td valign="top">Love this shot!  Don''t know how I missed it before!  Very cool.</td>', 'Love this shot!  Don''t know how I missed it before!  Very cool.', '2005-09-26 12:09:20.000000', NULL, 0),
